From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Reinsmidt <735251+ericreinsmidt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 22:50:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Pin banks can go back to 3.3 V: sunxi_sel_pio_mode only ever
 set a bank's 1.8 V mode bit and never cleared it, so a bank once in 1.8 V
 mode stayed there with its supply switched to 3.3 V under it

---
 drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c
index 75c58f312..511155a95 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c
@@ -1771,6 +1771,9 @@ int sunxi_sel_pio_mode(struct pinctrl *pinctrl, u32 pm_sel)
 			bank = pins[i] / PINS_PER_BANK;
 			raw_spin_lock_irqsave(&pctl->lock, flags);
 			tmp = readl(pctl->membase + GPIO_POW_MODE_SEL);
+			/* Cleared as well as set: OR alone left a bank in 1.8 V
+			 * mode for good, its supply switched to 3.3 V under it */
+			tmp &= ~(1 << bank);
 			tmp |= (pm_sel << bank);
 			writel(tmp, pctl->membase + GPIO_POW_MODE_SEL);
 #ifdef CONFIG_SUNXI_PIO_POWER_SEL
